-- The utility types the compiler builds from the fields of a struct, class or interface.
-- Each is declared here so it can be found, completed and documented; what it stands for is
-- worked out by the compiler.

--- Every field of the struct, class or interface `T`, each made optional.
---
--- ```nebra
--- local changes: Partial<User> = { name = "Ada" }
--- ```
declare type Partial<T>

--- Every field of the struct, class or interface `T`, each without `nil`.
---
--- ```nebra
--- local complete: Required<Options> = { verbose = true, depth = 2 }
--- ```
declare type Required<T>

--- The fields of the struct, class or interface `T` that `K` names: one name or a union of names.
---
--- ```nebra
--- local preview: Pick<User, "name" | "email"> = { name = "Ada", email = "ada@example.com" }
--- ```
declare type Pick<T, K>

--- Every field of the struct, class or interface `T` but those `K` names: one name or a union of names.
---
--- ```nebra
--- local draft: Omit<User, "id"> = { name = "Ada", email = "ada@example.com" }
--- ```
declare type Omit<T, K>
